      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the weight of one bowling ball, we need to follow a step-by-step approach using the information provided in the problem.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - Seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes.\n   - Two canoes together weigh 56 pounds.\n\n2. **Calculate the weight of one canoe:**\n   - Since two canoes weigh 56 pounds, the weight of one canoe is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Weight of one canoe} = \\frac{56 \\text{ pounds}}{2} = 28 \\text{ pounds}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Determine the combined weight of the seven bowling balls:**\n   - We know that seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes. Therefore, the combined weight of the seven bowling balls is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Combined weight of seven bowling balls} = 3 \\times \\text{Weight of one canoe} = 3 \\times 28 \\text{ pounds} = 84 \\text{ pounds}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Find the weight of one bowling ball:**\n   - Since seven bowling balls together weigh 84 pounds, the weight of one bowling ball is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Weight of one bowling ball} = \\frac{84 \\text{ pounds}}{7} = 12 \\text{ pounds}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the weight of one bowling ball is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) pounds.",
